WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.639
OK, today we have another concept question.

00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:11.279
A contractor is building footings loaded equally in two different kinds of soil.

00:00:11.279 --> 00:00:17.240
The project's timeline is lax, and mitigating structural failures is being prioritized,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:22.160
so the goal is to have both footings achieve their long-term settlement at roughly the same

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.879
amount of time before continuing with the project.

00:00:25.879 --> 00:00:30.839
Which footing should be built first?

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:36.320
So our options we can see over here for footing one and footing two are that footing

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.159
one is built on clay, and footing two is built on sand.

00:00:41.159 --> 00:00:45.320
So footing one should be built before footing two.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.560
Footing two should be built before footing one.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.799
Both footing should be built at the same time, and it does not matter when either footing

00:00:53.799 --> 00:00:55.280
is built.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:02.480
Again, this is just a conceptual question, and the answer will be the first answer.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.000
Footing one should be built before footing two.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.280
And the only reason for this is that the long-term settlement for clay will take longer than

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.120
the long-term settlement for sand.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.879
So building the footing on clay should begin first to give it more time to achieve its long-term

00:01:18.879 --> 00:01:19.879
settlement.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.879
And that's pretty much it for this problem.
